#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:49
msgid "system journal.persistent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:51
msgid ""
"Enables or disables journal persistence. Can be `true` or `false`. If "
"persistent journals were previously enabled by this setting, changing the "
"value to `false` will **delete all saved logs**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:53
msgid "Example to enable the journal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:54
msgid "snap set system journal.persistent=true\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:60
msgid "system proxy.{http,https,ftp}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:62
msgid ""
"These options may be set to change the proxies to be used by the system when "
"communicating with external sites that speak the respective protocols:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:64
msgid ""
"snap set system proxy.http=\"http://<proxy_addr>:<proxy_port>\"\n"
"snap set system proxy.https=\"http://<proxy_addr>:<proxy_port>\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:71
msgid "system pki.certs.custom"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:73
msgid ""
"Enables custom certificate management with the following options (replace "
"`<name>` with the certificate name):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:75
msgid ""
"**pki.certs.custom.\\<name>.content**: sets the certificate payload. This "
"option must be set first to register the certificate in the database, and "
"the `<name>` used in the option becomes the initially registered certificate "
"name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:76
msgid ""
"**pki.certs.custom.\\<name>.name**: changes the registered certificate name "
"after the certificate content has been set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:77
msgid ""
"**pki.certs.custom.\\<name>.state**: sets the certificate state to `blocked` "
"or `accepted`. If not explicitly set, the default state is `accepted`. "
"Setting the state to `unset` removes the certificate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:79
msgid ""
"The following example sets the certificate content from a PEM-encoded "
"certificate file, changes the certificate name, and blocks the certificate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:81
msgid ""
"snap set system pki.certs.custom.<name>.content=\"$(cat my-root.crt)\"\n"
"snap set system pki.certs.custom.<name>.name=new-name\n"
"snap set system pki.certs.custom.<name>.state=blocked\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:87
msgid "To remove the certificate, set its state to `unset` or unset it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:89
msgid ""
"snap set system pki.certs.custom.<name>.state=unset\n"
"snap unset system pki.certs.custom.<name>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:94
msgid "Use `snap get` to retrieve the list of custom certificates:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:96
msgid "snap get system pki.certs.custom\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:100
msgid ""
"Any custom certificate change requires restarting the snap for it to see the "
"updated system certificates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:104
msgid "ⓘ Available since snapd _2.79_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:106
msgid "system refresh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:108
msgid ""
"There are four system-wide options that are used to manage how updates are "
"handed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:110
msgid "**refresh.timer**: defines the refresh frequency and schedule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:111
msgid ""
"**refresh.hold**: delays the next refresh until the defined time and date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:112
msgid ""
"**refresh.metered**: pauses refresh updates when network connection is "
"metered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:113
msgid ""
"**refresh.retain**: sets how many revisions of a snap are stored on the "
"system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:115
msgid ""
"The following example asks the system to only refresh snaps between 4.00am "
"and 7.00am, and 7.00pm and 10:10pm:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:117
msgid "snap set system refresh.timer=4:00-7:00,19:00-22:10 \n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:121
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Controlling updates <how-to-guides-work-with-snaps-manage-"
"updates>` for further details on how the above options are used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:123
msgid "system homedirs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:125
msgid ""
"Allows a snap’s user data to be stored in a user’s home location other under "
"`/home`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:127
msgid "snap set system homedirs=<destination-directory>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:131
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Home directories outside of ‘/home’ <interfaces-home-outside-"
"home>` for further details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:133
msgid "ⓘ Available since snapd _2.59_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:135
msgid "system interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:137
msgid ""
"Permits specific interfaces' options to be changed. Currently, only the {ref}"
"`x11 interface<interfaces-x11-interface>` and option {ref}`auto-connection "
"<explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>` are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:139
msgid ""
"**interface.allow-auto-connection**: configure auto-connection rules for the "
"interface, options are `{false|true|verified}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:140
msgid "`false` or `true` controls whether auto-connections are permitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:141
msgid ""
"`verified` means that only snaps carrying a snap declaration can auto-"
"connect this interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:143
msgid ""
"The following example would configure the `x11` interface to deny all auto-"
"connections:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:146
msgid "snap set system interface.x11.allow-auto-connection=false\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:150
msgid "ⓘ Available since snapd _2.73_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:152
msgid "system resilience.vitality-hint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:154
msgid ""
"This option adjusts the Linux kernel's out-of-memory ([OOM](https://"
"www.kernel.org/doc/gorman/html/understand/understand016.html)) killer "
"behaviour for specific snap services."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:156
msgid ""
"By default, all snap services have the same value for systemd's "
"`OOMScoreAdjust`. By passing a list of snaps ordered by decreasing "
"importance to the `resilience.vitality-hint` system option, the order is "
"respected if snap processes are killed in low memory situations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:158
msgid ""
"The list of snaps need to be as string containing comma separated snap "
"instance names in decreasing order of importance, such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:160
msgid "snap set system resilience.vitality-hint=snapA,snapB,snapC\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:164
msgid ""
"In the above example, services inside `snapA` are the **least likely** to be "
"killed in _out of memory_ situations, followed by services in `snapB`, "
"services in `snapC`, and then the services in all the other snaps not "
"referenced by the `vitality-hint` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:167
msgid ""
"ⓘ  Snaps added to `resilience.vitality-hint` are still _more likely_ to be "
"killed than the snap daemon, snapd, itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:170
msgid "system service.console-conf.disable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:172
msgid ""
"May be set to _true_ on devices running Ubuntu Core to disable the console-"
"conf system configuration wizard that is launched by default when booting an "
"initialised Ubuntu Core image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:174
msgid "snap set system service.console-conf.disable=true\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:178
msgid ""
"This option is defined in the {ref}`gadget snap <reference-development-yaml-"
"schemas-the-gadget-snap>` and cannot be changed at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:182
msgid "system service.ssh.disable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:184
msgid "Can be set to _true_ to disable the SSH service at startup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:186
msgid "snap set system service.ssh.disable=true\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:192
msgid "system service.ssh.listen-address"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:194
msgid "Specifies the local address that the SSH daemon should listen on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:196
msgid ""
"Can be a comma separated list of hostnames, IPs or ports. When set, the SSH "
"[ListenAddress](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man5/sshd_config.5.html) "
"configuration is configured accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:198
msgid ""
"Port configuration needs to be in the following format: `:<port-number>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:200
msgid ""
"snap set system service.ssh.listen-address=:8022\n"
"snap set system service.ssh.listen-address=myhost\n"
"snap set system service.ssh.listen-address=192.168.1.2,myhost,foo:8022\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:206
msgid "ⓘ Available since snapd _2.59_ and only on Ubuntu Core 20 or later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:208
msgid "system snapshots.automatic.retention"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:210
msgid ""
"{ref}`Automatic snapshot <how-to-guides-manage-snaps-create-data-snapshots>` "
"retention time is configured with the `snapshots.automatic.retention` system "
"option. The default value is 31 days, and the value needs to be greater than "
"24 hours:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:212
msgid "snap set system snapshots.automatic.retention=30h\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:215
msgid "To disable automatic snapshots, set the retention time to `no`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:217
msgid "snap set system snapshots.automatic.retention=no\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:221
msgid ""
"ⓘ Disabling automatic snapshots will *not* affect preexisting, automatically "
"generated snapshots, but only those generated by subsequent snap removals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:223
msgid "ⓘ Automatic snapshots require snap version _2.39+_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:225
msgid "system store.access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:227
msgid ""
"When set to `offline`, prevents the system for initiating connections to the "
"Store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:229
msgid "snap set system store.access=offline\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:233
msgid ""
"Prevention includes explicit actions, such as installing a snap, and "
"automatic actions, such as periodic refreshes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:235
msgid "Unsetting the parameter restores the default access to the store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:237
msgid "snap unset system store.access\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:241
msgid "ⓘ Available since snapd _2.61_ and only on Ubuntu Core."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:243
msgid "system store-certs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:245
msgid ""
"A custom SSL certificate can be added to snapd's trusted certificates pool "
"for the store communication with the `store-certs.<name>=<value>` system "
"option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:247
msgid "To add a certificate, enter the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:249
msgid "snap set system store-certs.cert1=\"$(cat /path/to/mycert)\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:253
msgid "A certificate can be removed with _unset_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:255
msgid "snap unset system store-certs.cert1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:259
msgid "system swap.size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:261
msgid "Sets the swap size for the base system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:263
msgid ""
"Value can be any integer multiple of a megabyte that is either larger than "
"or equal to 1 MB, or 0 for no swap enabled:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:265
msgid "snap set system swap.size=200M\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:269
msgid ""
"This option is typically defined in the {ref}`gadget.yaml <reference-"
"development-yaml-schemas-the-gadget-snap>` file when building an Ubuntu Core "
"image:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:271
msgid ""
"defaults:\n"
"  system:\n"
"    swap:\n"
"      size: 200M\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:280
msgid "system system.hostname"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:282
msgid "May be used to set the static hostname of the host:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:284
msgid "snap set system system.hostname=\"new_name\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:290
msgid "system system.disable-backlight-service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:292
msgid "May be set to _true_ to disable the backlight service:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:294
msgid "snap set core system.disable-backlight-service=true\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:301
msgid "system system.kernel.cmdline-append"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:303
msgid ""
"Dynamically add permitted kernel boot parameters to the default kernel "
"command line on devices using the GRUB bootloader and with [Ubuntu Core "
"20/22](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/uc20/inside) or later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:305
msgid "snap set system system.kernel.cmdline-append=”opt1=val1 opt2=val2”\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:308
msgid ""
"Proposed kernel boot parameters are verified against an _allow list_ in the "
"{ref}`gadget snap <reference-development-yaml-schemas-the-gadget-snap>`. See "
"{ref}`gadget.yaml <reference-development-yaml-schemas-the-gadget-snap>` for "
"further details on the list syntax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:310
#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:328
msgid ""
"This options requires the system or device to be manually restarted. The "
"system will not restart automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:312
msgid "Consider using `system.kernel.dangerous-cmdline-append` instead if:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:314
msgid ""
"the gadget snap on your device is either the pc-gadget or pi-gadget, as the "
"allow list isn’t defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:315
msgid "you need to add kernel boot parameters without any verification filter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:318
msgid "system system.kernel.dangerous-cmdline-append"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:320
msgid ""
"Dynamically add any kernel boot parameters to the default kernel command "
"line on devices using the GRUB bootloader with [Ubuntu Core 20](https://"
"ubuntu.com/core/docs/uc20/inside) or later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:322
msgid ""
"snap set system system.kernel.dangerous-cmdline-append=”opt1=val1 "
"opt2=val2”\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:326
msgid ""
"This system setting is considered **dangerous** because any boot parameter "
"is permitted, potentially making devices vulnerable. To add only permitted "
"or filtered options, see `system.kernel.cmdline-append` above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:330
msgid "system system.kernel.printk.console-loglevel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:332
msgid "Override the console log level with a number between 0 and 7."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:334
msgid ""
"The configuration will be stored in `/etc/sysctl.d/99-snapd.conf` and the "
"default value is **4**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:336
msgid "Example to set the log level to 1:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:338
msgid ""
"$ snap set system system.kernel.printk.console-loglevel=1\n"
"$ cat /etc/sysctl.d/99-snapd.conf \n"
"kernel.printk = 1 4 1 7\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:346
msgid "system system.motd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:348
msgid ""
"Ubuntu Core systems come with a default message of the day. From Ubuntu Core "
"24 onwards, the message of the day can be customized from the defaults "
"configuration section in the {ref}`gadget.yaml <reference-development-yaml-"
"schemas-the-gadget-snap>` file to set a custom message available since first "
"boot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:350
msgid ""
"defaults:\n"
"  system:\n"
"    system:\n"
"      motd: |\n"
"        Welcome to Ubuntu Core\n"
"        Wish you a great day\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:359
msgid "Message of the day can also be configured in a running system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:361
msgid ""
"snap set system system.motd=\"$(printf \"Welcome to Ubuntu Core\\nWish you a "
"great day\")\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:365
msgid ""
"Here `printf` is used to handle the backslash-escaped characters such as "
"newline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:367
msgid "To set a custom message from a file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:369
msgid "snap set system system.motd=\"$(cat /path/to/custom/motd)\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:373
msgid ""
"The custom message can be removed with _unset_ which will reset to the "
"default message of the day:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:375
msgid "snap unset system system.motd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:381
msgid "system system.network.netplan"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:383
msgid ""
"On systems that support [Netplan](https://netplan.io/), such as Ubuntu Core "
"20 and 22, snapd can both query and configure the Netplan key and value "
"notation through its _get_ and _set_ system options commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:386
msgid ""
"$ snap get -d system system.network.netplan\n"
"{\n"
"        \"system.network.netplan\": {\n"
"                \"network\": {\n"
"                        \"ethernets\": {\n"
"                                \"enp0s2\": {\n"
"                                        \"dhcp4\": true\n"
"                                }\n"
"                        },\n"
"                        \"version\": 2\n"
"                }\n"
"        }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:401
msgid ""
"Netplan key names and properties reflect a device's specification, "
"capabilities and configuration. The `network.ethernets.enp0s2` device listed "
"above, for example, could be `eth0` or another network device name. Equally, "
"a device with wireless capabilities would present key value configuration "
"options beneath `system.network.netplan.network.wifi`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:403
msgid ""
"For example, the following output is typical of a static network "
"configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:405
msgid ""
"{\n"
"        \"system.network.netplan\": {\n"
"                \"network\": {\n"
"                        \"ethernets\": {\n"
"                                \"enp0s2\": {\n"
"                                        \"addresses\": [\n"
"                                                \"10.0.2.15/24\"\n"
"                                        ],\n"
"                                        \"gateway4\": \"10.0.2.2\",\n"
"                                        \"nameservers\": {\n"
"                                                \"addresses\": [\n"
"                                                        \"8.8.8.8\",\n"
"                                                        \"8.8.4.4\"\n"
"                                                ],\n"
"                                                \"search\": []\n"
"                                        }\n"
"                                }\n"
"                        },\n"
"                        \"version\": 2\n"
"                }\n"
"        }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:430
msgid ""
"The following `snap set` command could be used to change the `gateway4` "
"address in the above configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:432
msgid ""
"snap set system "
"system.network.netplan.network.ethernets.enp0s2.gateway4=10.0.2.1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:436
msgid ""
"See [Netplan reference](https://netplan.io/reference) for details on the key "
"and value pairs used for network configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:438
msgid "ⓘ Available since snapd _2.55.4_ and only on Ubuntu Core."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:440
msgid "system system.power-key-action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:442
msgid "Defines the behaviour of the system when the power key is pressed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:444
msgid "May be set to one of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:446
msgid "ignore"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:447
msgid "poweroff"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:448
msgid "reboot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:449
msgid "halt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:450
msgid "kexec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:451
msgid "suspend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:452
msgid "hibernate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:453
msgid "hybrid-sleep"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:454
msgid "lock"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:456
msgid ""
"To set the system power button behaviour to _hibernate_, for example, enter "
"the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:458
msgid "snap set system system.power-key-action=hibernate\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:464
msgid "system system.timezone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:466
msgid ""
"May be used to set a time zone value, as typically found in `/usr/share/"
"zoneinfo`, such as `America/Chicago`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:468
msgid "snap set system system.timezone=\"America/Chicago\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:472
msgid "To see the current timezone settings, use the `snap get -d system`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:474
msgid ""
"$ snap get -d system\n"
"{\n"
"        \"experimental\": {\n"
"                \"hotplug\": true,\n"
"                \"layouts\": true\n"
"        },\n"
"        \"refresh\": {\n"
"                \"last\": \"2017-05-25T09:03:58.664837614+01:00\",\n"
"                \"retain\": 2\n"
"        },\n"
"        \"seed\": {\n"
"                \"loaded\": true\n"
"        },\n"
"        \"system\": {\n"
"                \"timezone\": \"America/Chicago\"\n"
"        }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:496
msgid "system tmp.size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:498
msgid ""
"Configures the default size for the `/tmp` mount point on Ubuntu Core "
"devices:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:500
msgid "snap set system tmp.size=<size>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:504
msgid ""
"Size can given as either bytes, megabytes or gigabytes: `<bytes>`, `<bytes/"
"2^20>M`, or `<bytes/2^30>G`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:506
msgid ""
"To set the `/tmp` mount point to a size of 2GB, for example, run the "
"following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:508
msgid "snap set system tmp.size=2G\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:512
msgid "Use `snap get` to retrieve the current size:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:514
msgid "snap get system tmp.size\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:518
msgid "To set to `/tmp` to the default size, remove any custom setting:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:520
msgid "snap unset system tmp.size\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:523
msgid "By default, `/tmp` is set to use 50% of physical RAM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:527
msgid "system users.create.automatic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:529
msgid ""
"When _true_, permits the system to create users automatically from a valid "
"[system-user assertion](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/reference/assertions/"
"system-user), such as an assertion stored on external storage (see [System "
"user](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/system-user) for more details). When "
"_false_, users can only created manually with _create user_ API calls:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:531
msgid "snap set system users.create.automatic=false\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:535
msgid "Default is **true**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:537
msgid "system users.lockout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:539
msgid ""
"When set to `True`, Ubuntu Core user accounts will be locked for 900 seconds "
"after 3 wrong passwords."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:541
msgid "Can be either `True` or `False`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:545
msgid "system watchdog.runtime-timeout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:547
msgid "Configures the system's hardware watchdog _runtime_ timeout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:549
msgid ""
"The watchdog runtime timeout is an interval during which the system manager "
"must contact the hardware watchdog to prevent a device from being "
"automatically rebooted. Usage of this feature requires corresponding "
"hardware support as the watchdog hardware, `/dev/watchdog` or the kernel "
"option `systemd.watchdog-device=`, will be programmed to automatically "
"reboot the system when not contacted within the specified timeout interval."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:551
msgid ""
"A valid value is a non-negative time duration in seconds, or suffixed with "
"`ms`, `min`, `h`, `d`, `w` for milliseconds, minutes, hours, days and weeks "
"respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:553
msgid "The following example will set the timeout to 1 minute:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:555
msgid "snap set system watchdog.runtime-timeout=1m\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:561
msgid ""
"The Raspberry Pi hardware watchdog timer is limited to a maximum timeout of "
"15 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:566
msgid "system watchdog.shutdown-timeout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:568
msgid "Configures the system's hardware watchdog _shutdown_ timeout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:570
msgid ""
"The watchdog shutdown timeout is an interval to permit a clean reboot of the "
"system. If the system fails to reboot within this interval, the watchdog "
"will forcibly restart the system to protect against failed or hanging "
"reboots. Usage of this feature requires hardware support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:572
msgid ""
"Note that the shutdown-timeout applies only to the second phase of a reboot, "
"after all regular services are terminated and the system and service manager "
"process has been replaced by the systemd-shutdown binary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:574
msgid ""
"As with the _watchdog runtime timeout_, a valid value is a non-negative time "
"duration in seconds, or suffixed with `ms`, `m`, `h`, `d`, `w` for "
"milliseconds, minutes, hours, days and weeks respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:576
msgid "The following example will set the timeout to 500 seconds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/system-options.md:578
msgid "snap set system watchdog.shutdown-timeout=500\n"
msgstr ""
